           <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,580.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>BONO</td>\n                <td>₦1,580.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,580.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,580.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,580.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,570.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,550.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,550.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NNPCL IPO Returns: Nigeria Revives Decade-Old Plan to List Oil Giant\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria has revived its long-delayed plan to list Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited (NNPCL) on the Nigerian Exchange Group (NGX) President Bola Tinubu renewed the commitment during a meeting with the leadership of NGX Group on August 6. The potential listing of NNPCL could provide a major boost to market depth, liquidity and the number of large-scale investable assets.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nnpcl-ipo-returns-nigeria-revives-decade-old-plan-to-list-oil-giant\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Rise After Iran Gives U.S. Conditions for Reopening Strait of Hormuz\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $84.37 a barrel, up 0.98%, while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $78.76, gaining 0.74%. Iran’s declaration that the Strait of Hormuz would remain closed until the United States meets a series of demands that go well beyond shipping arrangements.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-rise-after-iran-gives-us-conditions-for-reopening-strait-of-hormuz\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Crisis: Gain for Federal Government, Pain for Consumers\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The prolonged disruption of the Strait of Hormuz has created a difficult contradiction for Nigeria. Higher international oil prices can strengthen government revenue at a time when crude production is recovering. But the same global supply shock can expose consumers and businesses to higher energy and transportation costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-gain-for-federal-government-pain-for-consumers\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    MEST OS Is the Digital Operating System Every Fuel Retail Station Needs —Obinna Joshua Igwe\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    MEST OS is an all-in-one retail operations platform built for the downstream oil and gas sector. It centralises the management of single and multi-station fuel retail networks. The platform centralises reporting into one system, reducing reliance on multiple communication channels.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/mest-os-is-the-digital-operating-system-every-fuel-retail-station-needs-obinna-joshua-igwe\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Five Things to Know About Petroleumprice.ng Awards Nomination\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Petroleumprice.ng Recognition & Awards 2026 nomination process is currently open. Participants can nominate individuals and organisations across six categories in Nigeria's downstream petroleum industry. Nominations close on September 15, 2026 and all entries must be submitted before the deadline. Top five nominees in each category will qualify for the next stage of the process.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/five-things-to-know-about-petroleumpriceng-awards-nomination\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
